<p>SE Ranking Website Audit is a cloud crawler within the SE Ranking platform. It can suit teams that want scheduled crawls, raw URL data, reporting and other search tools in one account. Treat its scores and priorities as navigation aids; confirm the underlying URL and intended state before changing the site.</p>

<h2 id="what-is-se-ranking">What Is SE Ranking Website Audit?</h2>

<p><a href="https://seranking.com/website-audit.html" rel="noopener noreferrer">SE Ranking's product page</a> documents manual and scheduled crawls, JavaScript rendering, crawl comparison, raw crawl data, custom rules, exports and reporting. Availability and allowances depend on the current account and plan.</p>

<h2 id="audit-features">Set Up the Audit</h2>

<ol>
  <li>Define the host, subdomain or section that is in scope.</li>
  <li>Choose URL sources, exclusions, crawl depth and page limit.</li>
  <li>Enable JavaScript rendering only when important content or links require it.</li>
  <li>Set a schedule that matches publishing and release frequency.</li>
  <li>After the crawl, reconcile discovered URLs with sitemaps and a known page inventory.</li>
</ol>

<h2 id="health-score">Use the Health Score as a Summary</h2>

<p>The score summarises conditions in the completed crawl according to SE Ranking's rules. It cannot measure content usefulness, commercial value or the full search state. Compare it only between like-for-like crawls and open the issue details when it changes.</p>

<h2 id="issue-categories">Verify Issue Categories</h2>

<p>Review crawlability, indexability, status, directives, canonicals, links, resources, metadata and performance as separate evidence groups. Sample every affected template. Then create one task for the shared cause with the full affected-URL export attached.</p>

<p>For Core Web Vitals, identify whether a result is lab data or Chrome UX Report field data. A crawler finding cannot replace real-user measurement for INP.</p>

<h2 id="white-label-reports">White-Label Reports</h2>

<p><a href="https://seranking.com/white-label.html" rel="noopener noreferrer">SE Ranking documents white-label options</a>. Verify the exact plan entitlement for PDF branding, automated reports, platform branding, custom domain and client access. Export a sample with a test client account before committing.</p>

<h2 id="se-ranking-vs-competitors">SE Ranking vs Competitors</h2>

<p>Compare SE Ranking with <a href="/website-audit-tools/semrush/">Semrush</a> and <a href="/website-audit-tools/ahrefs/">Ahrefs</a> when the wider cloud platform matters, or with <a href="/website-audit-tools/screaming-frog/">Screaming Frog</a> when local configuration and extraction are central. Compare evidence and workflow on the same URLs, not proprietary issue totals.</p>

<h2 id="who-it-is-best-for">Who It Fits</h2>

<p>It fits an owner, consultant or agency that needs recurring cloud audits and reporting in the SE Ranking workspace. Test another product if a required integration, crawl state, permission model or export is absent from the current trial.</p>

<h2 id="pricing">Pricing and Allowances</h2>

<p>SE Ranking changes plan names, prices and limits over time. The official page states that pages per project and account vary by plan. Check <a href="https://seranking.com/subscription.html" rel="noopener noreferrer">current subscription terms</a> for pages, projects, seats, history, API and white-label access.</p>

<p><small>Product facts checked against SE Ranking's official Website Audit and white-label pages on 11 September 2026.</small></p>

